{
  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: We have only one data point (config_004: multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, concat → acc 0.536, 0.56 GPU hrs). This is moderate and we don't yet know which design axis is most limiting. Question: config_031 is a clean single-variable ablation of config_004, swapping only the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l while keeping scvi_n200, singleprofile, and concat fusion identical. This directly tests whether a stronger, pre-trained vision transformer encoder meaningfully improves multimodal accuracy over a standard CNN. Why this is the best next step: the image encoder is likely the largest single lever for cellular profiling performance (ViT-L captures richer spatial/morphological features than ResNet-50), and isolating this variable gives us a clear signal to guide the remaining 7 experiments. If it substantially improves over 0.536, we can exploit the ViT-L direction; if not, we redirect effort toward RNA encoder or multiprofile aggregation. Expected relative cost: moderate — imagenet_vit_l is roughly 2-3× the compute of resnet50, but with no aggregation overhead (singleprofile), total training should be around 1.0–1.5 GPU hours, well within budget."
}

